-- Waystone: hunter pets. The bestiary (families, what each is good for, where to tame which
-- beast), the best pet for your level, and what to teach your pet next.
--
-- Data: PetData.lua (generated by scripts/build-pets.mjs from Wowhead Forever: every tameable
-- beast with its level, zone, attack speed and the ability ranks it teaches, and every pet
-- ability rank with its pet level and training point cost). The family numbers below are the
-- classic family modifiers; Wowhead Forever does not list them.
--
-- Classic rules used:
--   * a pet's damage per hit does not depend on its attack speed, so a faster beast is more DPS:
--     Wowhead Forever lists the speed as "Faster Attack I-VII" (1.7 s down to 1.0 s; normal 2.0)
--   * a family modifier multiplies damage, armor and health (cat 1.10 damage, turtle 1.13 armor...)
--   * you can tame a beast up to your own level; a pet learns an ability rank from Beast Training
--     after you have tamed a beast that knows that rank, for training points (pet level × loyalty)

local _, WA = ...
local L = WA.L
WA = WA or {}
local P = {}
WA.Pets = P

